  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent an admission fee. Then we have $X\u223cN(\\mu ,{0.7}^{2}),$ and we want to find the mean $\\mu .$ \n\nWe know that $P(0.75\\mu <X<1.25\\mu )=0.94.$ First, we convert this to a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.75\\mu <X<1.25\\mu ) & =0.94 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<1.25\\mu ) & =0.94 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<1.25\\mu ) & =0.47 \\\\ P(X<\\mu )+P(\\mu <X<1.25\\mu ) & =0.5+0.47 \\\\ P(X<1.25\\mu ) & =0.97\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1.25\\mu ) & =0.97 \\\\ P(Z<\\frac{0.25\\mu }{0.7}) & =0.97 \\\\ \u03a6(\\frac{0.25\\mu }{0.7}) & =0.97 \\\\ \\frac{0.25\\mu }{0.7} & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.97)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.97)\u22481.8808.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.25\\mu }{0.7} & =1.8808 \\\\ 0.25\\mu  & =1.31656 \\\\ \\mu  & =\\frac{1.31656}{0.25} \\\\  & \u22485.27.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
